--[[
	BossBrawl  -  Sagat vs Zenithega  (spectacle version)
	LocalScript / executor script for "I Wanna Test The Game".

	How it works
	  * Turn the toggle ON and start the Zenithega fight (or turn it on mid-fight).
	  * Sagat appears at the arena's PlayerSpawn, standing on the floor.
	  * Your character disappears and rides inside Sagat, so everything Zenithega aims
	    at you goes to him. You can't be hurt; you get control back when the brawl ends.
	  * Sagat walks, jumps and uses his own moves: Tiger Shots, Omega Shots, Sanic lobs,
	    jumping Tiger Shots and the Tiger Uppercut. His shots home in on her, and when she
	    floats out of reach he leaps up to her height and hits her in the air.
	  * Attacks that must be stopped with a charged shot (Death, Heaven's Wrath, her heal,
	    her shield, swords, Zundamon) are countered by Sagat with charged shots.
	  * He jumps over her dashes and lunges, hops over floor spikes, and runs out from
	    under Zangief when he drops in during her final phase.
	  * Master Spark: low beam -> he double-jumps over it; high beam -> he crouches.
	  * Swords: he hits HER with a charged shot, which ends the attack.
	  * He parries her shockwaves, shoots her apples down (and double-jumps to drag them
	    up when they get close), and climbs the wall to dodge the opening laser.
	  * Final phase: infinite jumps - he flies up to her and fights her in the air.
	  * When Sagat wins, Zenithega plays her defeat animation and stays down, and Sagat
	    walks back to the start of the arena and laughs. Use "Leave fight" to respawn.
	  * Sagat deals REAL damage to Zenithega through her own TakeDamage: her health bar
	    drops and she goes into phase 2 and her final phase normally.
	  * The killing blow is never dealt: when a final-phase hit would finish her, Sagat
	    wins and she stays alive. Her health stays locked (nobody else can damage her)
	    until that fight ends, so a brawl fight can't clear the stage. To actually beat
	    her, fight her normally without the brawl.
]]

